  "database": "rschema_0303",
  "nl_text": "The database schema \"rschema_0303\" is used to store information about projects, their acceptance criteria, sprints, messages, stories, and tasks. The schema consists of six tables: Project, Acceptance_Criteria_Table, Sprint, Message_Event, Story, and Task.\nThe Project table contains information about each project, including its creation time, project ID, project description, project name, and update time. The Acceptance_Criteria_Table contains information about the acceptance criteria for each project, including the acceptance criteria ID, description, and status.\nThe Sprint table contains information about each sprint, including its end time, project ID, sprint ID, sprint name, start time, status, and foreign key to the Project table. The Message_Event table contains information about each message event, including its creation time, message event ID, message reference, project ID, subject, update time, version, and foreign key to the Project table.\nThe Story table contains information about each story, including its description, project ID, sprint ID, status, story ID, story points, title, and foreign keys to the Project and Sprint tables. The Task table contains information about each task, including its description, status, story ID, task ID, title, and foreign key to the Story table.\nThe schema enforces domain integrity by specifying data types for each column and whether they allow null values. It also enforces entity integrity by defining primary keys and unique constraints for each table. Referential integrity is enforced by defining foreign keys and specifying update and delete rules for each foreign key. Finally, the schema includes indexes and constraints to optimize query performance.",
  "gold_question": "Business Requirements Description:\nThis database is for an Agile Development Management System used to manage stories (requirements), tasks, sprints (iterations), and acceptance criteria within a project. The primary features include:\n1.Manage Stories (Requirements): Create and edit stories, including story descriptions, status, story points, and titles. Assign stories to specific projects and sprints.\n2.Manage Tasks: For each story, create and assign tasks, including task titles, descriptions, and status.\n3.Manage Sprints (Iterations): Create and manage sprints within a project. Each sprint belongs to a project and includes a name, start time, end time, and status. Assign stories to specific sprints.\n4.Manage Acceptance Criteria: For each story, create acceptance criteria, including criteria ID, description, and status. Track and manage the acceptance criteria for stories.\n5.Message Event Management: Record message events related to specific topics, including event ID, subject, message reference, version, creation time, and update time. This is used for messaging and event recording within the project.\nThrough these features, the system helps teams better manage and track project progress, ensuring each story and task is completed on time and meets the acceptance criteria.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0303.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0303\nCREATE TABLE `project` (\n  `project_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `project_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `project_description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `creation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `update_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`project_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `acceptance_criteria_table` (\n  `acceptance_criteria_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `project_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`acceptance_criteria_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `acceptance_criteria_table_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`project_id`) REFERENCES `project` (`project_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `sprint` (\n  `sprint_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `project_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `sprint_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `start_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `end_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`sprint_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `sprint_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`project_id`) REFERENCES `project` (`project_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `message_event` (\n  `message_event_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `project_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `subject` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `message_reference` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `creation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `update_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `version` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`message_event_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `message_event_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`project_id`) REFERENCES `project` (`project_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `story` (\n  `story_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `project_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `sprint_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `story_points` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`story_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `story_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`project_id`) REFERENCES `project` (`project_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `story_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`sprint_id`) REFERENCES `sprint` (`sprint_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `task` (\n  `task_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `story_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`task_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `task_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`story_id`) REFERENCES `story` (`story_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
